<title>USA: TABLE - York Financial Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - York Financial Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>YORK, Pa. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended  Twelve months ended</p>
<p>					June 30	     June 30</p>
<p>				1997	1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p>		    (Dollars in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p> Net interest income  $9,063     $8,938    $35,853    $34,975</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses</p>
<p>				 248	  500	2,424	2,300</p>
<p>Net interest income after Provision</p>
<p>  for loan losses	8,815	8,438     33,429     32,675</p>
<p> Other income	    2,339	2,004	8,696	8,630</p>
<p> Other expenses	  7,374	6,393     31,163     24,450</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>			     3,780	4,049     10,962     16,855</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes</p>
<p>			     1,020	1,602	3,875	6,512</p>
<p> Net income		2,760	2,447	7,087     10,343</p>
<p>Per share data:</p>
<p> Net income		 0.38	 0.35	 0.99	 1.49</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>  shares	     7,301,248  7,020,112  7,179,592  6,960,058</p>
<p>NOTE: York Financial Corp has assets of $1,162,400,000 at June 30, 1997, as compared to assets of $1,109,800,000 at June 30, 1996, and operates through its principal subsidiary York Federal Savings and Loan Association which has 20 branches in South Central Pennsylvania and two branches in Harford County, Maryland.</p>
<p>York Financial is an independent financial institution headquartered in York County, Pennsylvania.</p>
<p>(( --New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
